# [CVE-2018-10095] Dolibarr XSS Injection vulnerability


## Description

Dolibarr is an "Open Source ERP & CRM for Business" used by many
companies worldwide.

It is available through [GitHub](https://github.com/Dolibarr/dolibarr)
or as distribution packages (e.g .deb package).

**Threat**

The application does not handle user input properly, allowing
client-side JavaScript code injection (XSS).

**Expectation**

User input should be filtered to avoid arbitrary HTML injection.


## Vulnerability type

**CVE ID**: CVE-2018-10095

**Access Vector**: remote

**Security Risk**: high

**Vulnerability**: CWE-79

**CVSS Base Score**: 7.4

**CVSS Vector String**: CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:N/A:N


## Details

Checks are enforced on user input via the `test_sql_and_script_inject()`
function, which forbids some SQL keywords (e.g `union`, `create`,
`insert`) and some XSS-related strings (`onfocus`, for instance).

```php
main.inc.php

/**
 * Security: SQL Injection and XSS Injection (scripts) protection
(Filters on GET, POST, PHP_SELF).
 *
 * @param       string      $val        Value
 * @param       string      $type       1=3DGET, 0=3DPOST, 2=3DPHP_SELF
 * @return      int                     >0 if there is an injection
 */
function test_sql_and_script_inject($val, $type)
{
    $inj =3D 0;
    // For SQL Injection (only GET are used to be included into bad
escaped SQL requests)
    if ($type =3D=3D 1)
    {
        $inj +=3D preg_match('/updatexml\(/i',     $val);
        $inj +=3D preg_match('/delete\s+from/i',   $val);
        $inj +=3D preg_match('/create\s+table/i',  $val);
        $inj +=3D preg_match('/insert\s+into/i',   $val);
        $inj +=3D preg_match('/select\s+from/i',   $val);
        $inj +=3D preg_match('/into\s+(outfile|dumpfile)/i',  $val);
    }
    if ($type !=3D 2) // Not common, we can check on POST
    {
        $inj +=3D preg_match('/update.+set.+=3D/i',  $val);
        $inj +=3D preg_match('/union.+select/i',   $val);
        $inj +=3D preg_match('/(\.\.%2f)+/i',      $val);
    }
    // For XSS Injection done by adding javascript with script
    // This is all cases a browser consider text is javascript:
    // When it found '<script', 'javascript:', '<style', 'onload\s=3D' on
body tag, '=3D"&' on a tag size with old browsers
    // All examples on page: http://ha.ckers.org/xss.html#XSScalc
    // More on
https://www.owasp.org/index.php/XSS_Filter_Evasion_Cheat_Sheet
    $inj +=3D preg_match('/<script/i', $val);
    $inj +=3D preg_match('/<iframe/i', $val);
    $inj +=3D preg_match('/Set\.constructor/i', $val);    // ECMA script 6
    if (! defined('NOSTYLECHECK')) $inj +=3D preg_match('/<style/i', $val);
    $inj +=3D preg_match('/base[\s]+href/si', $val);
    $inj +=3D preg_match('/<.*onmouse/si', $val);       // onmousexxx can
be set on img or any html tag like <img title=3D'...' onmouseover=3Dalert(1=
)>
    $inj +=3D preg_match('/onerror\s*=3D/i', $val);       // onerror can be
set on img or any html tag like <img title=3D'...' onerror =3D alert(1)>
    $inj +=3D preg_match('/onfocus\s*=3D/i', $val);       // onfocus can be
set on input text html tag like <input type=3D'text' value=3D'...' onfocus =
=3D
alert(1)>
    $inj +=3D preg_match('/onload\s*=3D/i', $val);        // onload can be
set on svg tag <svg/onload=3Dalert(1)> or other tag like body <body
onload=3Dalert(1)>
    $inj +=3D preg_match('/onclick\s*=3D/i', $val);       // onclick can be
set on img text html tag like <img onclick =3D alert(1)>
    $inj +=3D preg_match('/onscroll\s*=3D/i', $val);      // onscroll can be
on textarea
    //$inj +=3D preg_match('/on[A-Z][a-z]+\*=3D/', $val);   // To lock event
handlers onAbort(), ...
    $inj +=3D preg_match('/&#58;|&#0000058|&#x3A/i', $val);       //
refused string ':' encoded (no reason to have it encoded) to lock
'javascript:...'
    //if ($type =3D=3D 1)
    //{
        $inj +=3D preg_match('/javascript:/i', $val);
        $inj +=3D preg_match('/vbscript:/i', $val);
    //}
    // For XSS Injection done by adding javascript closing html tags
like with onmousemove, etc... (closing a src or href tag with not
cleaned param)
    if ($type =3D=3D 1) $inj +=3D preg_match('/"/i', $val);       // We
refused " in GET parameters value
    if ($type =3D=3D 2) $inj +=3D preg_match('/[;"]/', $val);     // PHP_SE=
LF
is a file system path. It can contains spaces.
    return $inj;
}
